<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zaire</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1971">1971</a>–<a href="/years/1997">1997</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zaire was the official name of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a> from 1971 to 1997, adopted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mobutu-sese-seko">Mobutu Sese Seko</a> as part of his campaign of 'authenticity'. Under Mobutu's one-party rule the country, rich in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>, cobalt and diamonds, suffered from corruption and economic decline. In 1996–1997 an invasion by rebels under Laurent-Désiré Kabila, backed by Rwanda and Uganda, overthrew Mobutu, and the country resumed the name Democratic Republic of the Congo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zaire.jpg" alt="Zaire" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Moyogo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Zaire_(1971%E2%80%931997).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…overthrew the elected government of Salvador Allende, and Argentina in 1976, and repeatedly in Nigeria, Ghana and many other African states; independence leaders banned rival parties; and personal rulers such as Mobutu Sese Seko in <b>Zaire</b> (1965–1997) and Ferdinand Marcos in the Philippines (1965–1986) held power for decades.</blockquote><a href="/government/dictatorship">Dictatorship · Through History</a></li><li><blockquote>Party membership is usually a minority of the population, though Mobutu Sese Seko’s <b>Zaire</b> enrolled every citizen in its ruling movement.</blockquote><a href="/government/one-party-state">One-party state · How It Works</a></li></ul></section>
